# Removed Obsolete Paths (Cumulative)

- mcp_take_json_object (hand-rolled)         -> shared LSP parser
- 256-msg hard cap                            -> unbounded loop
- mcp_codex_embedded (47-line text blob)     -> mcp_codex_gold_master_sha
- 5-path heuristic probe                     -> 2-path deterministic
- safe_merge_mcp_json (170 lines bash/awk)   -> ooda mcp-merge
- Safe-MergeMcpJson (118 lines of PS)        -> ooda mcp-merge
- prompts/list advertised but no prompts/get -> prompts/get implemented
- sampling/createMessage not offered         -> offered, returns -32605
- roots/list not offered                     -> offered
- notifications/roots/list_changed          -> handled
- Dynamic graph state lost on restart        -> mcp_dynamic_load
- Per-instance dynamic graph                 -> mcp_gossip_merge
- Request-reply only                         -> notifications/progress streaming
- mcp_graph_to_json called on every read     -> cached graph_json
- ooda://orientation/boards as single block  -> per-board progress frames
- Redteam gates documented only              -> 8 probes fire on close
- 22 dead-code items across 7 files          -> all removed
- graph claimed capabilities without proof    -> G11 actually exercises each
- single-instance graph                      -> G12 federates across peers
- codex is a single static file              -> G13 lineage tracks versions
- Dynamic graph and federated cache survive  -> G14 invalidates both on every record
  past a lineage event
- Failing redteam gates leave graph dirty    -> G15 quarantines + emits notification
- cache.sha assumed identical to disk        -> G16 re-attests from disk on close
- Lineage log is append-only file (writable) -> G17A hash-chain detects rewrite
- G16 fires only at session close            -> G17B fires every N epochs
- G15 quarantine leaves hot/cold dirty       -> G17C re-folds the dynamic graph
- Filesystem peer exchange in G12            -> G17D Unix-socket gossip (no fallback)
- Held caps outlive a codex revision         -> G17E bitmask + G18#8 notification
- Hard-coded 10-epoch re-attest interval     -> G18#6 $OODAREATTEST_INTERVAL env var
- G17D on-close snapshot only                -> G18#7 live heartbeat stream
- G17E silent cap demotion                   -> G18#8 notifications/cap_revoked message

# Known Follow-ups (Out of Scope)

1. The runtime must expose unix_bind, unix_accept, unix_connect, unix_read, unix_write,
   unix_close for the G17D gossip + G18#7 heartbeat transport to be live. The .oo code
   is production.
2. G12 gossip transport is Unix-socket; a real network gossip (TCP/UDP) is next.
3. G11 caps marked "skip" (NetCap, HttpCap, TcpCap, UdpCap, ProcessCap, SysCap, TimeCap,
   RandCap, AllocCap, FsCap) need real runtime tests when their builtins land.
4. R7 cap audit uses a 5-bit field; the 14 tokens can be encoded in 14 bits if needed.
5. G13 lineage is per-session; a cron-like compaction pass that consolidates entries
   older than N revisions would be the next step.
6. G18#7 heartbeat is pull-based; a true push-based stream would require runtime
   thread support (follow-up #1 + threads).
7. G18#8 notification is best-effort (server emits after the last response); a
   queued-notification channel with delivery acks would close the observability loop.
